<prov:Activity rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#GenerationActivity">
  <rdfs:label>Ontology generation by OntoGeneration Agent (step 23)</rdfs:label>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#RefinedTerms"/>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#ProposedAxioms"/>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#ProposedTests"/>
  <prov:generated rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#OntologyDraft_iteration0"/>
  <prov:wasInformedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#TestGenerationActivity"/>
  <prov:wasAssociatedWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
  <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
  <prov:hadPlan rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#GenerationPrompt"/>
  <prov:qualifiedAssociation>
    <prov:Association>
      <prov:agent rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
      <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/odrl_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
    </prov:Association>
  </prov:qualifiedAssociation>
  <vaem:rationale>The ontology models all supplied classes, individuals, and properties to answer each atomic competency question. Classes form a closed taxonomy with Duty and Prohibition as subclasses of Rule. Individuals are declared as instances of their respective classes. Properties carry explicit domain/range axioms matching the proposed specifications, and general properties (ruleRelation, prohibitionDutyLink) are coined per step 6 to unify shared domains/ranges. All entities map directly to the competency questions they serve.</vaem:rationale>
</prov:Activity>

